From 5ee45e6e56978fef39e899f1804c1ecd60b988a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 06:27:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] perf(core): skip unused detached path in vehicle update
 copies

VehicleExtraData.copy(pathUpdateIndex) detached-copied every PathData of the
vehicle's path for each client update, only for the constructor to wrap it as
the copy's immutablePath before clearing path and re-adding the needed subset.
Its only caller, Client.update, places the copy in a VehicleUpdate that is
serialized from path. Redirect copyPath in copy() to an empty list; the
serialized update and all other fields are unchanged. The compatibility test
checks the call sequence, the single caller and that no update consumer reads
immutablePath.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TD7PJ5R7t7hM3ymeeqXP4H
